From 60ce2a71f748969d519697b147fdb52fed1e2a30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:55:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/52] HIP/RDNA3 multi-column MMVQ: buffer-resource loads,
 per-type occupancy, Q6_K pipelining, transposed DPP reduction

- byte-offset loaders for Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/IQ4_XS: one 16-byte header load for dm+scales (Q4_K/Q5_K), one 8-byte
  header (IQ4_XS), 8-byte scale word (Q6_K); rows/columns are raw buffer resources in SGPRs, so the loop advances
  two shared 32-bit offsets instead of a 64-bit VGPR address per load
- amdgpu_waves_per_eu per (type, ncols) at 5-8 columns (HIP's __launch_bounds__(n, 1) pinned it to the default, which
  makes the scheduler wait on every load); 2-4 columns and ncols 1 unchanged (n=1 ISA identical)
- Q6_K at 5 columns: next iteration's raw weights loaded before the current ones are unpacked
- epilogue: one transposed butterfly (permlanex16 + DPP row_xmask) for all ncols*rows sums, one store per lane
All bitwise identical to the previous kernels (all multi types, ncols 1-8, full and partial last row block).
